The cersrt Java recognition package is based on Wayeb by Elias Alevizos,
as distributed in https://github.com/ElAlev/cer-srt at commit
688cb0617131024aa2538d0ddc6b5d500c3aaaea.

Upstream attribution and licensing terms are preserved in
META-INF/licenses/wayeb-LICENSE.md. See docs/cer-srt.md for scope and changes.

The corecer.exceptions, corecer.execution, corecer.parser, corecer.runtime
packages and corecer.util.StringUtils are derived from
https://github.com/CORE-cer/CORE-paper, experiments branch at commit
de8166902f664fd7ceec06ffa3c9a136825de07a.
Their original edu.puc.core packages have been consolidated into corecer.
The upstream GPL-3.0 license is preserved in
META-INF/licenses/core-cer-LICENSE.txt. CORE experiment queries originate from
https://github.com/CORE-cer/CORE-paper-experiments at commit
69c4ca1afeceefbed0682d75b1bf031599f9f785.
See docs/core-cer.md for retained components, local adaptations, and scope.
